DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       _N_o_t_e:  this  page  describes  the raw Linux system call interface.  The
       wrapper function provided by _l_i_b_a_i_o  uses  a  different  type  for  the
       _c_t_x___i_d argument.  See VERSIONS.

       The  iioo__ccaanncceell() system call attempts to cancel an asynchronous I/O op‐
       eration previously submitted with iioo__ssuubbmmiitt(2).  The _i_o_c_b argument  de‐
       scribes the operation to be canceled and the _c_t_x___i_d argument is the AIO
       context to which the operation was submitted.  If the operation is suc‐
       cessfully canceled, the event will be copied into the memory pointed to
       by _r_e_s_u_l_t without being placed into the completion queue.

